---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import {articles} from '../../data/site.js'; export function getStaticPaths(){return articles.map(article=>({params:{slug:article.slug},props:{article}}))}; const {article}=Astro.props; const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title={`${article.title} — Trade Avata`} description={article.excerpt}><section class="page-hero"><div class="shell article-body"><span class="eyebrow">{article.category}</span><h1 class="page-title">{article.title}</h1><p class="lead">{article.excerpt}</p><p style="font-size:10px;color:#8ea6bc;margin-top:12px">{article.read} read · Trade Avata Learning</p></div></section><section class="section"><article class="shell article-body"><h2>Start with a clear purpose</h2><p>Good trading decisions become easier to review when the process is written in plain language. Define what you are looking for, what would invalidate the idea and how much risk the trade is allowed to carry before entering.</p><h2>Separate setup quality from outcome</h2><p>A profitable trade can still be poorly executed, and a losing trade can still follow a strong plan. Review the evidence, the decision and the execution separately so the result does not become the only thing you judge.</p><h2>Use consistent evidence</h2><p>Record the same core information each time: market context, setup, confirmation, risk, execution notes and the lesson after the trade. Consistent records make comparisons more useful inside Analytics and Journal.</p><div class="notice" style="margin:28px 0">Trade Avata educational content is for learning and review. It does not provide personalized financial advice.</div><a class="button" href={`${base}articles/`}>← Back to Articles</a></article></section></BaseLayout>
